      "id": "L0_INDEPENDENT_PROTOCOL_SCOPE_TRANSPORT",
      "statement": "Independent scope verification establishes the explicit finite task model as a candidate superset of TASK_TO_DELEGATION_GRAPH_001 with exact environment and candidate-visible information. Independent temporal transport pins that relation to the exact current candidate, oracle, and Opus55 family-protocol blobs. The current behavioral-registry delegation row is semantically identical to the historical row independently checked by that transport."
    },
    {
      "id": "L1_FINITE_SEARCH_COMPLETENESS",
      "statement": "Because each declared step may appear at most once, only fact-adding applicable unused steps are extended, and the step set is finite, the candidate search tree is finite and reaches every simple executable fact-producing sequence. Exhaustion with no schedulable goal is therefore a complete impossibility result within the declared finite model."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2_GLOBAL_PLAN_OPTIMALITY",
      "statement": "All admitted step costs are finite and nonnegative. The candidate priority queue orders paths by total cost, task count, then lexical sequence and returns a goal only after schedulability succeeds. Therefore the first returned goal is the globally minimal schedulable goal under the frozen objective."
    },
    {
      "id": "L3_EXHAUSTIVE_ORACLE_EQUIVALENCE",
      "statement": "The frozen oracle enumerates every subset and permutation of available steps, rejects invalid prerequisite sequences, rejects unschedulable plans, and minimizes the identical cost/task-count/lexical key. Thus candidate and oracle select the same plan for every contract in the proof domain."
    },
    {
      "id": "L4_MINIMUM_WAVE_SCHEDULE",
      "statement": "The candidate scheduler breadth-first searches completed-task subsets through every resource- and capability-feasible worker matching. Since worker availability and resource capacities reset each wave and future readiness depends only on completed tasks, first completion has minimum wave count."
    },
    {
      "id": "L5_EVIDENCE_INVARIANTS",
      "statement": "Every selected or completed step has a unique evidence owner or the solver fails closed; terminal fan-in includes the evidence of all selected and completed work, so duplicate/conflicting work and lost-evidence critical invariants cannot be hidden by a successful result."
    },
    {
      "id": "L6_REPLANNING_CLOSURE",
      "statement": "Every supported live receipt transforms the same finite explicit task state and solve_after_receipt reruns the same exact solver. L1-L5 therefore hold after each supported receipt as well as initially."
    }
